---
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Legal" description="Terms for use of LocalMax and for benchmark submissions.">
  <section class="wrap prose">
    <div class="eyebrow">Legal</div>
    <h1>Legal</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Read this before you run LocalMax or submit a result. Use of the software and the
      website means that you accept these terms.
    </p>

    <div class="callout">
      <strong>Read the source first.</strong> LocalMax runs on your computer. It reads
      hardware data and starts an inference server. All source code is public at
      <a href="https://github.com/pavel4ai/localmax.net">github.com/pavel4ai/localmax.net</a>.
      Examine it before you run it. Do not run software that you have not examined.
    </div>

    <h2>Submissions are voluntary</h2>
    <p>
      You are not required to submit a result. You start each run. You start each
      submission. Command <code>localmax inspect</code> shows the full content of a
      submission before upload. Nothing goes to LocalMax until you approve it.
    </p>

    <h2>You accept all risk</h2>
    <p>
      You use LocalMax at your own risk. A benchmark puts a large load on your hardware for a
      long time. This can cause high temperatures, high power use, instability, data loss, or
      damage to hardware.
    </p>
    <p>
      You are responsible for your hardware, your cooling, your power supply and your data.
      You are responsible for backups. Make sure that your system is safe to operate at full
      load before you start a run.
    </p>

    <h2>You are responsible for permission</h2>
    <p>
      Submit results only from hardware that you own or that you have permission to
      benchmark. Do not submit a result from a system under a confidentiality agreement or an
      embargo. You are responsible for compliance with the licence of each model and each
      data set that a benchmark uses.
    </p>

    <h2>Submitted data becomes public</h2>
    <p>
      An accepted result is public and permanent. LocalMax publishes it under the Creative
      Commons Attribution 4.0 licence, and copies it into a public Git history. You give
      LocalMax an irrevocable licence to publish the measured data, the system configuration
      data and the evidence that you submit.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can request removal. See <a href="/privacy">Privacy</a>. Removal from Git history
      occurs only for exposed secrets or personal data.
    </p>

    <h2>No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      LocalMax is supplied "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied. This
      includes, but is not limited to, warranties of merchantability, fitness for a purpose,
      and non-infringement.
    </p>
    <p>
      Results come from the public. A verification state describes the completeness and the
      internal consistency of the evidence. It does not prove that a value is correct. It
      does not prove that an operator was honest. Do not use this data as the only basis for
      a purchase, an engineering decision or a publication.
    </p>

    <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the maximum extent that the law permits, LocalMax, its owners, its maintainers, its
      contributors and its agents are not liable for any damage. This includes direct,
      indirect, incidental, special, consequential, exemplary and punitive damage. It
      includes damage to hardware, loss of data, loss of profit, loss of use and business
      interruption. This applies even if LocalMax knew that such damage was possible.
    </p>

    <h2>Indemnity</h2>
    <p>
      You agree to indemnify LocalMax, its owners, its maintainers, its contributors and its
      agents, and to hold them harmless. This applies to all claims, damages, losses,
      liabilities, costs and legal fees that result from:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>your use of the software or the website;</li>
      <li>a result that you submit;</li>
      <li>your breach of these terms;</li>
      <li>your breach of a law or of the rights of another party.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Removal of content</h2>
    <p>
      LocalMax can remove or annotate any result at any time, for any reason, and without
      notice. Reasons include fraud, a breach of a third-party licence, exposure of personal
      data, and a request from the contributor.
    </p>

    <h2>Trademarks</h2>
    <p>
      NVIDIA, GeForce, RTX and DGX are trademarks of NVIDIA Corporation. Other product names
      are the trademarks of their owners. LocalMax has no relationship with, and no
      endorsement from, these companies.
    </p>

    <h2>Licences</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Source code: Apache-2.0.</li>
      <li>Result data: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0.</li>
      <li>Benchmark inputs: each asset keeps its own licence. The profile records it.</li>
      <li>Model weights: each model keeps its own licence. LocalMax does not distribute weights.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      These terms can change. The Git history of this page records every change. Continued
      use after a change means that you accept the new terms.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Legal: <a href="mailto:legal@localmax.net">legal@localmax.net</a>.
      Privacy and removal: <a href="mailto:privacy@localmax.net">privacy@localmax.net</a>.
      Security: <a href="https://github.com/pavel4ai/localmax.net/security/advisories/new">private advisory</a>.
    </p>

    <p class="muted small">
      This page is written in Simplified Technical English. It is not legal advice.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .prose { max-width: 720px; padding: 56px 24px 40px; }
  .prose h1 { font-size: 2.1rem; margin: 12px 0 16px; }
  .prose h2 { margin: 40px 0 12px; padding-top: 20px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .prose p, .prose li { color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .prose ul { padding-left: 20px; display: grid; gap: 8px; margin: 0 0 16px; }
  .prose code { background: var(--surface-2); padding: 1px 5px; border-radius: 3px; font-size: 0.88em; }
  .prose a { color: var(--text-primary); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-strong); }
  .callout {
    border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--surface-1);
    padding: 18px 20px;
    margin: 24px 0 8px;
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }
  .small { font-size: 12.5px; }
</style>
